# Redoubt LW-M7-37: clean an interrupted session before the next one browses.
#
# LibreWolf deletes cookies, site data and cache whenever the browser closes
# (desktop.cfg privacy.sanitize.sanitizeOnShutdown). Fenix deletes only from its
# explicit Quit menu item, and even there does not wait for Gecko's clearData
# callbacks, so a session that was swiped away or killed kept everything.
# On every cold start with "Delete browsing data on quit" on, run the selected
# categories before any engine session exists, awaiting each Gecko deletion.
# Engine sessions are held by a second instance of the uBO startup middleware
# (ubo-preinstall.patch) until cleanup has finished; a failure or the 30 s bound
# is logged and browsing continues, and the next start retries. Tabs are removed
# only after restore completes, so restore cannot bring them back.
# Requires ubo-preinstall.patch. Per-site cookie retention is not implemented.
#
diff --git a/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Components.kt b/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Components.kt
--- a/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Components.kt
+++ b/mobile/android/fenix/app/src/main/java/org/mozilla/fenix/components/Components.kt
@@ -237,6 +237,8 @@ class Components(private val context: Context) {

     val uboPreinstaller by lazyMonitored { LibreWolfUboPreinstaller(context) }

+    val startupCleanup by lazyMonitored { LibreWolfStartupCleanup(context) }
+
     val addonManager by lazyMonitored {
         AddonManager(core.store, core.engine, addonsProvider, addonUpdater)
     }
